{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"7afd1d2b0c207cdeb761bebd4d0ac5605bc3d30b35aeb8a2dabdcf140ab93190","digest":{"component_or_area":"code-review gate / LLM runner model resolution","key_entities":["code-review.yaml","PydanticAIRunner.run","resolve_model","RunnerAgentStep.run","gate_dispatch.py","llm/runner.py","llm/usage_log.py","req.config.model","cfg.model","_effective_config","ContextVar","model_class","model_ladder"],"problem_keywords":["code-review gate","model class","per-step model","wiring","per-call override","runner configuration","LLM model routing"],"propositions":["Code-review gate declares per-step model classes in code-review.yaml but all declarations are silently ignored at runtime; every step executes with the single cfg.model instead.","PydanticAIRunner.run discards req.config.model and resolves from self._config, dropping the per-step override that RunnerAgentStep carefully computed.","Usage logging does not record step id or declared model class, making it impossible to attribute LLM calls to steps or verify declarations are honoured.","A fix at the runner layer (substituting req.config.model into cfg before resolution) makes all per-step model declarations effective across code-review, plan-review, and completion gates."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787884636684767001,"uuid":"083b3ed2-14bd-4d1f-9277-9bf678517edb"}